---
// Prototype: terms rewritten for the open source first site. Fixes the live /terms, which puts the
// plugin under MPL-2.0 (it is GPL), and drops the paid tiers. Throwaway, not linked.
import DocPage from "@/components/proto/DocPage.astro";

export const prerender = true;

const LAST_UPDATED = "October 1, 2026";
---

<DocPage title="Terms - Loopress" kicker={`terms · last updated ${LAST_UPDATED}`} heading="Terms of use." lede="Short version: it's open source, it's alpha, test before production.">
  <h2>Licenses</h2>
  <p>
    The CLI is licensed under the <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/">Mozilla Public License 2.0</a>,
    the WordPress plugin under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html">GPL</a>. Those
    licenses govern the code: you can read it, modify it and redistribute it under their terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Alpha</h2>
  <p>
    Loopress is in alpha. Commands, file formats and behaviours can change between releases. Keep
    your own backups, and try every change on a staging site before production.
  </p>

  <h2>Your sites, your credentials</h2>
  <p>
    Use Loopress only on sites you are allowed to administer. You are responsible for the
    Application Passwords you give the CLI, and you can revoke one at any time from the site's
    admin.
  </p>

  <h2>The Loopress console</h2>
  <p>
    The console (console.loopress.dev) is a hosted service, free during the alpha, with no uptime or
    durability guarantee. Don't abuse its infrastructure. We may suspend accounts that do, and you can
    delete yours at any time through the <a href="/proto/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Loopress is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the extent permitted by law, we are
    not liable for indirect or consequential damages, including data loss on a site you manage with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We update this page when the terms change, and the date at the top with it.</p>
</DocPage>
